course: dictionary
lesson: 10579
title: One word, many meanings: under
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word under has several meanings, so the sentence around it tells you which one it is. Ask yourself: is something below something else, is a number being talked about, or is a rule being followed?
explain: «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.» Here under means below: the glow was on the far side of the door, at the bottom edge. «Old diving bells kept people dry under water the same way.» Under water means below the surface of the water.
explain: With a number, under means less than that number, and it does not include the number itself. «Children under 5» means children younger than 5, so a child who is exactly 5 is not under 5. When under means ruled by or following a rule, as in «children have special rights under a United Nations agreement», it means controlled by, or set by, that rule.
explain: Under can also mean during, as in «the road is under repair», which means it is being repaired right now. To check your meaning, swap in a simple word such as below, less than, following or during, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Under means below something, or covered by it.
fact: Under means less than a number, and does not include that number: children under 12 are aged 11 or younger.
fact: Under can mean controlled by or following a rule, as in «under a king» or «under the rules».
fact: Under can mean during, as in «the road is under repair», which means being repaired right now.
fact: Phrases like «under the bed», «under water», «under control» and «under construction» each use under in a slightly different way.
exercise: «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.» What does under mean here? | Less than a number | Ruled by a king | During the night | *Below, on the far side of something
exercise: A sign says «children under 12 must sit in the back seat.» Can a 12-year-old be told to sit in the front? | No, because under means the same as over | *Yes, because under 12 does not include 12 itself | Only if the car is stopped | No, because 12 is under 12
exercise: «The road is under repair.» What does under mean here? | Ruled by the repairs | *During, as the repairs are happening now | Less than a repair | Below the road
test: «Children have special rights under a United Nations agreement.» What does under mean here? | During | Less than | Below | *Following the rules set by
test: «Ten dollars is the most I can spend, and this costs under 10 dollars.» What does under 10 dollars mean? | *Less than 10 dollars, and not 10 dollars itself | During the 10 dollars | Lying below 10 dollars on the floor | Ruled by 10 dollars
exam: Tom says under only means below. Is he right? | Yes, under only ever means below | No, under means above | Yes, but only in science lessons | *No, under can also mean less than a number, controlled by a rule, or during
